            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nPricey but good quality and nice ambience - Ops Director Willie's friendly!\nMay 2023 • Family\nBeauty in the Pot's from Singapore... and just like in Singapore, they're known to be a little pricier than competitors, but they're also known to deliver good quality food. \n\nMother's Day promotion was available to us when we visited --- they were giving away a free serving of US Wagyu Beef for spending above 2 million VND. I would say for the 2 million VND that we spent, the food we got would be sufficient for 4 to 5 adults. Like I said --- it'd be considered expensive by Vietnamese standard... but actually considered very well-priced (and really good quality in terms of their freshness) by Singapore's standard. Signature collagen soup base is a must-order!\n\nWe liked that they have private rooms, but they were limited - only one or two rooms. So reserve early if you want a private room. Nonetheless, almost all window-seats in here have pretty good views of the city's skyline. \n\nWe also liked that they have a kids' indoor soft play area with new toys. This play area's not as big as the ones Beauty in the Pot has in Singapore, but it is rather good as a free playground for the little guests of a restaurant here. The magnetic kids-safe entrance/exit door was easy to operate by any adults, so it was easier to get our kids.\n\nMet the Operations Director, Willie, and he was really friendly and hands-on, helping his staff and chatting with the customers in English, Chinese and Vietnamese, always looking cheerful. Cool chap.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 14, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
